canonicalize.c: keep DEST valid when xrealloc moves RPATH (upstream bug)

Origin: written for seed-forth's plumbing stage 2; later gnulib versions of
  canonicalize.c make the same correction (they keep the offset of DEST
  across the reallocation).
Why: for a relative name, canonicalize_filename_mode copies the working
  directory into RPATH, points DEST at its end, then grows RPATH to
  PATH_MAX with xrealloc but keeps using the old DEST.  When realloc
  moves the block (runtime/gcc-seed's realloc always moves on growth;
  glibc usually extends in place, which hides the bug) DEST points into
  freed memory, and `readlink -f RELATIVE-NAME' crashes.
Applied by: plumbing/stage2.kaem, with the patch 2.5.9 built just before
  coreutils (patch -p1 -i in the coreutils-5.0 tree).

--- coreutils-5.0/lib/canonicalize.c
+++ coreutils-5.0/lib/canonicalize.c
@@ -171,7 +171,9 @@
       dest = strchr (rpath, '\0');
       if (dest < rpath + PATH_MAX)
 	{
+	  size_t dest_offset = dest - rpath;
 	  rpath = xrealloc (rpath, PATH_MAX);
+	  dest = rpath + dest_offset;
 	  rpath_limit = rpath + PATH_MAX;
 	}
       else
